  "explain": [
    {
      "t": "intro",
      "es": "En el present simple, para <b>negar</b> y <b>preguntar</b> necesitamos unos <mark>ayudantes</mark>: <b>do</b> y <b>does</b>. El ayudante hace el trabajo difícil (llevar la <em>-s</em> de he, she, it), así que el verbo principal descansa: va siempre <b>tal cual, sin s</b>.",
      "en": "We need the helpers <b>do</b> / <b>does</b> for negatives and questions. The main verb stays in its base form.",
      "formula": [
        "I / you / we / they → *do / don't*",
        "he / she / it → *does / doesn't*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "title": "1 · Negativa",
      "title_en": "Negative",
      "icon": "⛔",
      "color": "red",
      "es": "Para negar ponemos <b>don't</b> (do not) con I, you, we, they y <b>doesn't</b> (does not) con he, she, it, <mark>delante del verbo</mark>. El verbo va <b>sin s</b>, porque la s ya está en doe<em>s</em>n't. ¡Nunca digas «I no like»!",
      "en": "Negative: <b>don't / doesn't</b> + verb (no -s). Never 'I no like'.",
      "formula": [
        "I / you / we / they + *don't* + verbo",
        "he / she / it + *doesn't* + verbo"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I <b>don't like</b> broccoli.",
          "es": "No me gusta el brócoli.",
          "icon": "🥦"
        },
        {
          "en": "We <b>don't go</b> to school on Saturdays.",
          "es": "No vamos al cole los sábados.",
          "icon": "🏫"
        },
        {
          "en": "Lucía <b>doesn't watch</b> cartoons.",
          "es": "Lucía no ve dibujos.",
          "icon": "📺"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "title": "2 · Preguntas",
      "title_en": "Questions",
      "icon": "❓",
      "color": "blue",
      "es": "Para preguntar ponemos <b>Do</b> o <b>Does</b> <mark>al principio</mark>, luego el sujeto y luego el verbo <b>sin s</b>. En español basta con la entonación («¿Juegas al tenis?»), pero en inglés ¡el ayudante es obligatorio!",
      "en": "Questions: <b>Do / Does</b> + subject + verb (no -s)?",
      "formula": [
        "*Do* + I / you / we / they + verbo + …?",
        "*Does* + he / she / it + verbo + …?"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "<b>Do</b> you <b>like</b> pizza?",
          "es": "¿Te gusta la pizza?",
          "icon": "🍕"
        },
        {
          "en": "<b>Do</b> they <b>live</b> in Madrid?",
          "es": "¿Viven en Madrid?",
          "icon": "🏙️"
        },
        {
          "en": "<b>Does</b> Leo <b>play</b> football?",
          "es": "¿Leo juega al fútbol?",
          "icon": "⚽"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "tip",
      "title": "La mochila de DOES",
      "title_en": "The does backpack",
      "es": "Imagina que <b>does</b> es una mochila: ¡lleva la <em>-s</em> dentro! Cuando aparece does o doesn't, la s ya va en la mochila y el verbo va ligero, sin s. <i>She plays → She doesn't play → Does she play?</i>",
      "en": "<b>Does</b> carries the -s, so the verb goes without -s."
    },
    {
      "t": "table",
      "title": "3 · Respuestas cortas",
      "title_en": "Short answers",
      "icon": "💬",
      "color": "teal",
      "head": [
        "Pregunta · Question",
        "Sí · Yes",
        "No"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Do you like fish?",
          "Yes, I <b>do</b>.",
          "No, I <b>don't</b>."
        ],
        [
          "Does he play tennis?",
          "Yes, he <b>does</b>.",
          "No, he <b>doesn't</b>."
        ],
        [
          "Does she speak English?",
          "Yes, she <b>does</b>.",
          "No, she <b>doesn't</b>."
        ],
        [
          "Does it bark?",
          "Yes, it <b>does</b>.",
          "No, it <b>doesn't</b>."
        ],
        [
          "Do we have PE today?",
          "Yes, we <b>do</b>.",
          "No, we <b>don't</b>."
        ],
        [
          "Do they walk to school?",
          "Yes, they <b>do</b>.",
          "No, they <b>don't</b>."
        ]
      ],
      "note": "En la respuesta corta <b>no</b> repetimos el verbo: <s>Yes, I like.</s> → Yes, I <b>do</b>. Y contestamos con pronombre: Does <i>Lucía</i>…? → Yes, <b>she</b> does.",
      "note_en": "Don't repeat the verb: Yes, I do. Answer with a pronoun."
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "title": "4 · ¡Solo una S por frase!",
      "title_en": "Only one -s",
      "icon": "🐍",
      "color": "purple",
      "es": "La <em>-s</em> de he, she, it aparece <mark>una sola vez</mark> en la frase, y siempre en la palabra que «manda»: en la afirmativa, en el verbo (She play<em>s</em>); en la negativa y en la pregunta, en el ayudante (She doe<em>s</em>n't play · Doe<em>s</em> she play?). ¡Nunca en los dos!",
      "en": "Only ONE -s per sentence: on the verb (affirmative) or on <b>does</b> (negative and question).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "She <b>doesn't like</b> milk. <i>(<s>likes</s>)</i>",
          "es": "No le gusta la leche.",
          "icon": "🥛"
        },
        {
          "en": "<b>Does</b> he <b>watch</b> TV? <i>(<s>watches</s>)</i>",
          "es": "¿Él ve la tele?",
          "icon": "📺"
        },
        {
          "en": "My dad <b>doesn't have</b> a car. <i>(<s>has</s>)</i>",
          "es": "Mi padre no tiene coche.",
          "icon": "🚗"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "title": "5 · Preguntas con Wh-",
      "title_en": "Wh- questions",
      "icon": "🔎",
      "color": "green",
      "es": "Con las palabras de pregunta (<b>What, Where, When, What time…</b>) el orden es: <mark>Wh- + do / does + sujeto + verbo</mark>. ¡El ayudante va justo detrás de la palabra de pregunta!",
      "en": "Wh- word + <b>do / does</b> + subject + verb?",
      "formula": [
        "*Where* + *do* + you + live + ?",
        "*What time* + *does* + Lucía + get up + ?"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "<b>Where do</b> you live? — In Madrid.",
          "es": "¿Dónde vives? — En Madrid.",
          "icon": "🏠"
        },
        {
